# DIBAY Global Input UX Parity HARD LOCK

**HARD LOCK (2026-08-10).** Full doc: `docs/dibay-global-input-ux-parity-hard-lock.md`.

## Core

**동일 UX 계약 ≠ 동일 inset 계산.**

Unify product outcomes only: focus not hidden, no over-push, no blank keyboard–CTA gap, CTA reachable, keyboard close restore, press/haptic semantics.

**Do not** unify raw bottom inset / safe-area / keyboard height / viewport / nav bar / orientation / iOS·Android resize / tablet·desktop layout into one formula or one hardcoded px.

## Architecture

`Capability → Orientation → Nav/Safe (measured) → Keyboard model → Platform Adapter → Form SSOT → Surface → Form`

Normalized outputs (`effectiveViewportTop/Bottom`, `effectiveBottomInset`, `keyboardOpen`, `keyboardOcclusion`, `safeBottom`, focus band) = **common interface**, adapter-computed per environment.

## DO NOT (without reopen)

- Shared raw `safeBottom + keyboardHeight` (or one formula) for all platforms  
- Hardcode 3-button / home-indicator px  
- Reuse portrait→landscape or phone→tablet geometry  
- UA-only keyboard mode; guess nav bar from device name  
- Assume Android/iOS visualViewport identical  
- Expand one-env PASS (e.g. Samsung Community) to Android / Global / CLOSED  

## Matrix

Samsung/Xiaomi × portrait/landscape × gesture/3-button; iPhone P/L; tablet P/L; Windows physical/OSK — each row independent. Unmeasured = **NOT_PROVEN**. FINAL **OPEN** until doc CLOSED criteria.

